</figure>
<div id="S5.SS3.p6" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S5.SS3.p6.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.SS3.p6.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Ablation on the number of converters.</span>
We also demonstrate the impact of stacking varying numbers of converters on depth estimation performance.
The results in Tab. <a href="#S5.T7" title="Table 7 ‣ 5.3 Ablation Studies ‣ 5 Experiments ‣ More Than Generation: Unifying Generation and Depth Estimation via Text-to-Image Diffusion Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7</span></a> show that stacking multiple converters to create a larger one is ineffective and even has negative effects.
We suspect this is due to the significant increase in model depth, making optimization extremely challenging.</p>
</div>
