</figure>
<div id="S5.SS3.p7" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S5.SS3.p7.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.SS3.p7.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Ablation on the initialization methods of the converter.</span>
We further investigate the impact of different initialization methods for the converter on the depth estimation performance.
The results in Tab. <a href="#S5.T8" title="Table 8 ‣ 5.3 Ablation Studies ‣ 5 Experiments ‣ More Than Generation: Unifying Generation and Depth Estimation via Text-to-Image Diffusion Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">8</span></a> show that initializing the converter with the pre-trained T2I block (the first T2I block of each group) consistently outperforms random initialization.
This initialization strategy enables the converter to process the input features seamlessly.</p>
</div>
